QA Butler — Your QA Automation Assistant Powered by Flutter + Serverpod
Automated diagnostics for flaky test failures — your personal assistant for QA
Problem
In real-world QA, 30–40% of automated test failures are false positives, caused by:
Expired test logins
Full disk space
API rate limits
Changed test data
QA engineers waste h8ours manually triaging these failures instead of focusing on real bugs.
Solution
QA Butler is a digital assistant for QA engineers that:
Intercepts test failures
Runs automated diagnostics powered by Serverpod
Outputs a probable root cause before human intervention
Think of it as a personal assistant that helps engineers triage flaky tests quickly, saving time and reducing frustration.
Features
List all available tests
Copy code
Bash
qa-butler list
Analyze test failures
Copy code
Bash
qa-butler analyze
Performs automated diagnostics and identifies likely causes of failures.
Easy setup with Serverpod backend
Handles the heavy lifting of data processing, simulating a real-world QA automation workflow.
Terminal prototype now, Flutter UI next
While the current prototype runs in the terminal, future versions will feature a Flutter dashboard to monitor tests and results visually.
How to Run
Clone the repository:
Copy code
Bash
git clone https://github.com/Eddiejoe33/flaky-test-butler.git
Navigate to the project folder:
Copy code
Bash
cd flaky-test-butler
Run the CLI commands:
Copy code
Bash
qa-butler list
qa-butler analyze
Impact
QA Butler reduces time spent on false positives, allowing engineers to focus on real bugs. By automating diagnostics, it acts as a reliable assistant for QA teams, helping streamline workflows and improve productivity.
